{"title":"2016 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(variant_of_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (variant of Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Lifting_the_exponent)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Lifting the exponent)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that is a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/1/45126ee832c210aa7ce19942672f321088f9abb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^4 - 11^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19ab4ad09bd0bbac54a9318560261c0d3690d645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\mbox{ }8\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\mbox{ }16\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\mbox{ }32\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\mbox{ }64\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\mbox{ }128$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we use difference of squares on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d824f811c590731046e9e35a28290a2d8f6a32a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^4 - 11^4 = (13^2)^2 - (11^2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"213\" height=\"19\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff707237c8a4354bc12b73e7524c514b5e6ff774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^4 - 11^4 = (13^2 + 11^2)(13^2 - 11^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"271\" height=\"19\" />. Using difference of squares again and simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/4/b94e47c9a4c74e0ec3736b845cc9a7452a093439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(169 + 121)(13+11)(13-11) = 290 \\cdot 24 \\cdot 2 = (2\\cdot 8 \\cdot 2) \\cdot (3 \\cdot 145)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"508\" height=\"18\" />. Realizing that we don't need the right-hand side because it doesn't contain any factor of 2, we see that the greatest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that is a divisor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/1/45126ee832c210aa7ce19942672f321088f9abb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^4 - 11^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7abbdfc3d001daa30891f622fc24a12a851f1608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~CHECKMATE2021\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28variant_of_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(variant_of_Solution_1)\">Solution 2 (variant of Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (variant of Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Just like in the above solution, we use the difference-of-squares factorization, but only once to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/544dac2f4d090ea7c54e56ef5c63a8e22e818ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^4-11^4=(13^2-11^2)(13^2+11^2).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"280\" height=\"21\" /> We can then compute that this is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/079c682247d919438805918eca6948bc8041ed7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48\\cdot290.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271e5c0834b85996130559b992606457ba65afd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$290=2\\cdot145$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" /> (we don't need to factorize any further as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d00d6cfbf7dab73af54367e971ffc25a4091499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$145$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is already odd) thus the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2cf40f8ceb7e0ef7fbe35f590c889dd513334b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$290$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f9364c8f955788a1d241514063b4dd3f73cb7ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^1=2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/240f1301069500434752823c15a5fb6989ecf2f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48=2^4\\cdot3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> so the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc64b7f73dad699e6c5567477631bd7d44dc8e8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4=16.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"17\" /> Hence, the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that is a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55ca033dd01150a65f824e3b6f92fe56f769e5d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^4-11^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b14798d539eeaaf20ae5cab9efbcbdcc0710fba9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot16=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~32}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"135\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:CHECKMATE2021\" title=\"User:CHECKMATE2021\">CHECKMATE2021</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Lifting_the_exponent.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Lifting_the_exponent)\">Solution 3 (Lifting the exponent)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Lifting the exponent)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90ca19a193aef5077a888ba406669429b8f48258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=13^4-11^4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> We wish to find the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f19a1449b18f2bc4be00bdf29b3c7c30c94d19b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_p(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> as the largest exponent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. In this problem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b803838ba4ded99f094071740c256527784b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>By the Lifting the Exponent Lemma on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3eaeef1cd9e05f077f756c05d9d4db1d30fd4c6a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[v_2(13^4-11^4)=v_2(13-11)+v_2(4)+v_2(13+11)-1\\]\" width=\"419\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/d/fbde7f22b34603f4e7c3d6e1a5d7708869e46602.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=v_2(2)+v_2(4)+v_2(24)-1\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/defc375128fbd98998388fc1661cc1b51b017280.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=1+2+3-1=5.\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, exponent of the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that divids <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55ca033dd01150a65f824e3b6f92fe56f769e5d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^4-11^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/21415a2eb558eb7c199a0382fcd50cbeda9299fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> so the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that divides this number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/e/c1e8af5492d5a43b3b968acf332d42e574c32826.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^5=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} 32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~CHECKMATE2021\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 4 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can simply take 13 to the 4th power, which is 28561. We subtract that by 11 to the 4th power, which is 14641 (You can use Pascal's Triangle to find this). Finally, subtract the numbers to get 13920. \n</p><p>To test the options, since we need the largest one, we can go from top down. Testing, we see that both D and E are decimals,\nand 32 works. So, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe05ce63674182a09ce9ba91648c2371deed383e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~32}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"71\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-themathgood\n</p><p><br />\nNote: This is not the fastest way, and is not recommended.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/1/45126ee832c210aa7ce19942672f321088f9abb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^4 - 11^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e569131f7bb505eb5220e4287b291df009617142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(13^2-11^2)(13^2+11^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"21\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84f97411dc99c8ae8d3422f250c088f8601b9484.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(169-121)(169+121)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee80f8aa7fd55bf5d8ff139f24eff558ca25c628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(48)(290)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> which has 5 factors of 2 making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe05ce63674182a09ce9ba91648c2371deed383e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~32}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"71\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ JasonDaGoat\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HISL2-N5NVg?t=3705\">https://youtu.be/HISL2-N5NVg?t=3705</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mZCOgH2kVuE\">https://youtu.be/mZCOgH2kVuE</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution 2 (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fWEwuLKZ7jY\">https://youtu.be/fWEwuLKZ7jY</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 8\">2016 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.a